---
import { sitePath } from '../lib/site-path';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { repository, sourceRoot } from '../lib/examples';
import { quickStart, astroExample } from '../lib/snippets';
---
<Layout title="Quick start — Foldkit Viz">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">A small beginning</p>
    <h1>From values to visuals.</h1>
    <p>Foldkit Viz gives you the geometry. You choose the rendering, styling and interaction.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="docs-layout">
    <nav class="docs-nav" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#installation">Installation</a><a href="#quick-start">Your first chart</a><a href="#primitives">The primitives</a><a href="#composition">Compose a chart</a><a href="#foldkit">Using FoldKit</a>
    </nav>
    <article class="docs-content">
      <section id="installation">
        <h2>Install the package.</h2>
        <p>Add Foldkit Viz to your project, then import the modules you need.</p>
        <div class="code-panel"><Code code="bun add @opsydyn/foldkit-viz" lang="sh" theme="github-dark" /></div>
        <p>Working in this monorepo? Use <code>workspace:*</code> for the dependency. The geometry functions are pure TypeScript and have no D3 dependency.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="quick-start">
        <h2>A scale. A shape. A chart.</h2>
        <p>Map values into coordinates with two linear scales, then turn the points into an SVG path.</p>
        <div class="code-panel"><Code code={quickStart} lang="ts" theme="github-dark" /></div>
        <p>In Astro, compute the path in frontmatter and render it directly. No browser JavaScript is needed for a static chart.</p>
        <div class="code-panel"><Code code={astroExample} lang="astro" theme="github-dark" /></div>
        <a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/examples/line/')}>Try the live line example <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </section>
      <section id="primitives">
        <h2>Take the pieces you need.</h2>
        <div class="module-grid">
          {[
            ['math/scale', 'Scales', 'Map domains to ranges.'],
            ['shape/line', 'Lines', 'Choose how points connect.'],
            ['shape/chord', 'Connections', 'Turn matrices into ribbons.'],
            ['shape/sankey', 'Flows', 'Lay out sources and destinations.'],
            ['shape/geo', 'Geography', 'Project features into SVG.'],
            ['math/bin', 'Distributions', 'Group values into intervals.'],
            ['chart/bars', 'Grouped and stacked bars', 'Project categories and series in either orientation.'],
            ['layout/wordcloud', 'Word cloud', 'Place measured words with deterministic spirals.'],
            ['layout/text', 'Text layout', 'Wrap measured labels without browser dependencies.'],
            ['foldkit/paint', 'SVG paint', 'Compose dot patterns, hatching and gradients.'],
          ].map(([module, name, description]) => <a href={sourceRoot + '/' + module + '.ts'}>
            <h3>{name} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></h3><p>{description}</p><code>{module}</code>
          </a>)}
        </div>
        <a class="text-link" href={repository + '/tree/main/packages/foldkit-viz'}>Full module reference <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </section>
      <section id="composition">
        <h2>Compose the chart around your data.</h2>
        <p><code>chart/cartesian</code> maps your records through accessors into shared geometry. <code>chart/theme</code> supplies semantic light and dark paints and stable series styles. The optional <code>foldkit/cartesian</code> adapter renders frames, axes, marks, annotations, tooltips, legends and data tables through your parent's builder.</p>
        <p>Choose layer order and replace the tooltip with a renderer receiving the original datum. Build colour mappings from stable series IDs before filtering; use symbols or dash patterns alongside colour. CSS variables and custom CSS colours pass through unchanged, with opacity set separately.</p>
        <p>These modules are unreleased workspace APIs. Download a live example for a complete independent project containing the compiled modules, shared source and current control settings.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/examples/scatter/')}>Inspect the composed scatter example <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </section>
      <section id="signal-exploration"><h2>Keep exploration in your Model.</h2><p>Coordinates, bounded viewport navigation and nearest-record inspection are pure workspace APIs. A native Foldkit Model owns brush, pan, zoom and pin state; scoped Mount streams acquire browser facts. <a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/examples/signals/')}>Explore the Signal desk →</a></p></section>
      <section id="new-layouts"><h2>More ways to compose.</h2><p>Bars, word cloud, text layout and SVG paint are unreleased workspace APIs. <a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/examples/bars/')}>Try grouped and stacked bars →</a> <a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/examples/wordcloud/')}>Try the word cloud →</a></p><p>Word cloud takes measured text bounds and returns coordinates plus any words that could not fit. Measure fonts in a Command, then render the pure layout as SVG. Text wrapping accepts your measurement function. Paint definitions take caller-owned IDs and colours, including CSS variables.</p></section>
      <section id="foldkit">
        <h2>Keep your model in charge.</h2>
        <p>For interactive FoldKit charts, keep selections and chart state in your Model, describe interactions with Messages, and update through the normal loop. The primitives compute geometry; your app owns effects and data loading.</p>
        <p>The library is tested with FoldKit 0.165.x and Effect 4.0.0. Astro integration and application server rendering belong to the separate <code>@opsydyn/astro-foldkit</code> package.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href={repository + '/tree/main/apps/web/src/apps/linked-charts'}>See the linked-charts application <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
